# SPDX-License-Identifier: GPL-2.0-only
Subject: [PATCH] fbdev: mdss: associate framebuffer with its platform device

The vendor probe allocates fb_info with a NULL parent. New Xorg fbdevhw checks
the framebuffer device's subsystem to distinguish PCI from platform devices;
without a parent, /sys/class/graphics/fb0/device/subsystem does not exist and a
working framebuffer is rejected. Supply the actual platform device to the
standard allocator, so registration exposes the expected device relationship.

--- a/drivers/video/msm/mdss/mdss_fb.c
+++ b/drivers/video/msm/mdss/mdss_fb.c
@@ -1173,7 +1173,7 @@
 	/*
 	 * alloc framebuffer info + par data
 	 */
-	fbi = framebuffer_alloc(sizeof(struct msm_fb_data_type), NULL);
+	fbi = framebuffer_alloc(sizeof(struct msm_fb_data_type), &pdev->dev);
 	if (fbi == NULL) {
 		pr_err("can't allocate framebuffer info data!\n");
 		return -ENOMEM;
